{"type":"standard","title":"Southern Zaza","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Southern Zaza</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3943996","titles":{"canonical":"Southern_Zaza","normalized":"Southern Zaza","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Southern Zaza</span></span>"},"pageid":75159289,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Zaza_DialectsMap-5.gif/330px-Zaza_DialectsMap-5.gif","width":330,"height":149},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Zaza_DialectsMap-5.gif","width":579,"height":262},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353879108","tid":"43fdf2fb-4e58-11f1-8032-eff7e22012a1","timestamp":"2026-05-12T23:14:03Z","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_Zaza","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_Zaza?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_Zaza?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Southern_Zaza"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_Zaza","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Southern_Zaza","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Southern_Zaza?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Southern_Zaza"}},"extract":"Southern Zaza, is one of the three primary dialects of the Zaza language, spoken by the Zaza people. The dialect is also referred to as Dımli, Dımıli or Dımılki, which are believed to be historically and linguistically derived from the words Daylam and Daylamite.","extract_html":"<p><b>Southern Zaza</b>, is one of the three primary dialects of the Zaza language, spoken by the Zaza people. The dialect is also referred to as <i>Dımli</i>, <i>Dımıli</i> or <i>Dımılki</i>, which are believed to be historically and linguistically derived from the words Daylam and Daylamite.</p>"}